  "_comment": [
    "Offer fixture for `remote/provision.sh --dry-run`. Shaped like a real POST /bundles/",
    "response; the values reflect the live market observed on 2026-08-30 (single RTX 5090s",
    "at $0.32-$0.35/hr, 32 GB, CUDA 13.0). No credentials and no account data.",
    "Most entries exist to be REJECTED, so the dry run exercises the filter rather than",
    "just the happy path: 9001 is bid-only (interruptible), 9002 has two GPUs, 9003 has",
    "reliability below 0.98, 9004 is over the rate ceiling, 9005 is not rentable, and 9006",
    "is a fallback-generation card. Only 9007 and 9008 should survive, and 9008 is cheaper,",
    "so provision.sh must select 9008.",
    "9011 is the cheapest offer here and passes every other filter, but its driver tops out at CUDA 12.2 -- too old for the cu128 wheels run_remote.sh installs. Rental 25 died on such a host with 'Error 804: forward compatibility was attempted on non supported HW', so it must be rejected and 9008 must still win.",
    "9006 is the fallback-generation card AND advertises `cuda_max_good` exactly 12.8 -- on the floor rather than above it, which has produced Error 804 on every rental that took such a host (33, 41, 42; 51 was cancelled by hand on sight). DF_MIN_CUDA is 12.9 for that reason, so 9006 must now be rejected and 9012 -- the same card one driver newer, and $0.02 dearer -- is what the fallback search must select."
  ],
